<title>TURKEY: Malta ship aground in Bosphorus, traffic unaffected.</title>
<headline>Malta ship aground in Bosphorus, traffic unaffected.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Maltese flagged freighter was grounded as it passed through the Bosphorus strait on Thursday, Istanbul port authorities said.</p>
<p>The 15,548 dwt Friendly, carrying 25,000 tonnes of steel from Odessa port in Ukraine to Alexandria in Egypt, ran aground near the northern end of the strait at around noon local time (1000 GMT), following a mechanical fault.</p>
<p>Port authorities said the accident had no effect on traffic in the Bosphorous, one of the world's busiest waterways.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
